```php
<template>
  <div>
    <h1>{{ message }}</h1>
  </div>
</template>

<script lang="ts">
import { defineComponent } from 'vue';

export default defineComponent({
  setup() {
    const message = 'Hello, world!';

    return {
      message,
      mounted() {
        console.log('Component mounted.');
      },
    };
  },
});
</script>
```
In this example, we have a simple composable component that displays a message. The `message` data property is defined in the `setup` function, and the `mounted` lifecycle hook is called when the component is mounted. The `console.log` statement in the `mounted` hook logs a message to the console to indicate that the component has been mounted.

